torum.jpg/330px-Jacobus_de_Voragine_Legenda_aurea_sanctorum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This 1688 edition of Jacobus de Voragine's Golden Legend (1260) was censored according to the Index Librorum Expurgatorum of 1707, which listed the specific passages of books already in circulation that required censorship.[26][27]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacobus_de_Voragine_Legenda_aurea_sanctorum.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/George_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_%2838562767202%29.jpg/500px-George_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_%2838562767202%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/George_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_%2838562767202%29.jpg/1280px-George_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_%2838562767202%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/George_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_%2838562767202%29.jpg/500px-George_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_%2838562767202%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"George Orwell statue at the headquarters of the BBC. A defence of free speech in an open society, the wall behind the statue is inscribed with the words \"If liberty means anything at all, it means the right to tell people what they do not want to hear\", words from George Orwell's proposed preface to Animal Farm (1945).[32]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeorge_Orwell_statue_-_BBC_London_(38562767202).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Lady_chatterley%27s_lover_1959_US_unexpurgated_edition.jpg/500px-Lady_chatterley%27s_lover_1959_US_unexpurgated_edition.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Lad